  "body": "## What and why\n\nComplete the remaining rotary-stack documentation in #1084. The initial rows already shipped in 9707408b7.\n\n- Name the exact `get_rotary_stack` readback fields and its tallest-stack and null rules.\n- State the setter's required arguments, refusals and undo/redo behavior.\n- List the rotary-subplate dimensions for both accessory tools.\n- State the placement tolerance and the resize pin check.\n- Add three focused documentation tests and a decision record.\n\nCurrent source requires both `setup` and `nose_to_axis` for the setter. Only the getter defaults to the active setup.\nNo Rust behavior, geometry, G-code, workflow or dependency changes.\nPR #4057 changes different rows in the same skill. This PR does not stack on it or change those rows.\n\n## Source verification\n\nChecked against c92b6c3fc0e08899381a79b8da0d75c79ddb481e. The named source and skill files are unchanged on upstream main aef12fea67e0082e7ba835a3d9fcade8e2c11eb0:\n\n- `mcp/rotary_tools.rs`: schemas, routing, readback and history.\n- `rotary_stack.rs`: tallest stack, standing height, layers and pin law.\n- `commands/setup_nose.rs`: validation, apply and invert.\n- `mcp/accessory_tools.rs`: shared dimensions and accessory commands.\n- `accessory/subplate.rs`: frame, dimensions and spacing tolerance.\n- `commands/fixture_plate.rs`: placement and resize checks.\n\n## Checks and limits\n\n- PASS: `python3 -m unittest discover -s .claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/tests -v` — 10 tests.\n- The three new test methods fail against the original skill text, without test errors.\n- PASS: `git diff --check` and `git diff --cached --check` before commit.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: zero selected steps. No Rust tests ran; this is not a Rust test pass.\n- NOT RUN: `cargo xtask gate light`. Its dry-run selects six steps and 11 twins, with a release build. This is outside the documentation-only verification scope. AGENTS requires this lane at review; no pass is claimed.\n- No catalog, broad Rust, GUI or physical-machine checks ran. No runtime safety claim is made.\n\n## Process\n\nProcess change: yes\n\nCurrent AGENTS.md assigns the version bump and #681 announcement to the merging session.\nThis PR does not change PROCESS_VERSION or announce before merge.\n\nEffort: low\n\nChangelog: none\n\nFixes #1084\n",
